    "summary": "High‑energy ’82 Glenns Falls show – killer Jack Straw & blazing China Cat > Rider",
    "review": "The April 14, 1982 gig at the Glenns Falls Civic Center is a high‑octane snapshot of the early‑’80s Dead. The band kicks off with a punchy Jack Straw and rolls through a mixed first set that, while a bit uneven, still delivers a ferocious Deep Elem Blues and a thunderous Bertha. The second set flips the switch: a smoking China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider segue launches into a soaring Playin’ In The Band jam, and the night caps off with an unforgettable TLEO solo that has become a touch‑stone for fans of this era. Rare electric Deep Elem makes an appearance, and Brent’s jazzy space during Playin’ In The Band adds a dreamy layer to the improvisations.\n\nAcross the six recordings surveyed, the soundboard capture from Braverman (gd82-04-14.sbd.braverman.7629.sbeok.shnf) stands out as the most complete and sonically clear version – crisp guitars, solid mix, and full‑show coverage with only minor vocal balance quirks. Matrix and audience tapes also shine, especially for the TLEO solo and Deep Elem moments, but they suffer from typical early‑’80s bleed‑through or delay issues. For anyone looking to experience this night in its fullest fidelity, the Braverman SBD is the go‑to source.",
